From 846d08f21633692edad5c4744a5536f853722d3f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:47:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] rwatch: stand down while a firmware upgrade runs

stop_upgrade tears the firewall and the services down before the flash.
A probe tick inside that window (metal, 2026-10-27 12:20) logged
"FAILURE detected: warden-out-chain-missing", dumped an incident and
restarted rpunctd mid-flash. The generated script now exits at once while
/tmp/upgrade exists: stock writes it at the start of an upgrade, nothing
removes it before the reboot, and stock's watchdog and sched_daemon hold
off on the same file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1bb0f6b999a28b7f419ab7f15a41e30aac2cf102)
---
 release/src/router/rc/rwatch.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/release/src/router/rc/rwatch.c b/release/src/router/rc/rwatch.c
index 4e30229899e..5ce42661adb 100644
--- a/release/src/router/rc/rwatch.c
+++ b/release/src/router/rc/rwatch.c
@@ -78,6 +78,13 @@ static void rwatch_gen(void)
 	fputs(
 	  "#!/bin/sh\n"
 	  "# generated by start_rwatch - do not edit\n"
+	  /* 2026-10-27: stand down while a firmware upgrade runs. stop_upgrade tears the
+	   * firewall and the services down before the flash; a tick in that window
+	   * reported the missing Reaper chains as a FAILURE and restarted rpunctd
+	   * mid-flash. Stock writes /tmp/upgrade at the start of the upgrade and
+	   * nothing removes it before the reboot; its own watchdog and sched_daemon
+	   * hold off on the same file. */
+	  "[ -f /tmp/upgrade ] && exit 0\n"
 	  REAPER_NV_HELPER
 	  REAPER_NVS_HELPER
 	  "STATE=" RWATCH_STATE "\n"
-- 
2.25.1

